  "worked_solution": "According to Newton\u2019s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{(\\sqrt{t})}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the acceleration at $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(4) & =-\\frac{1}{4{(\\sqrt{4})}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4({2}^{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =ma(4) \\\\  & =64\\cdot -\\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the force is\n\n$$\n|F(4)|=|-2|=2\\,\\text{N}.\n$$",
